<h2>Final Verdict: The Best Entry Point for Strategy RPG Newcomers</h2>
<p>Putting the Reddit community’s insights together with our own analysis, it’s clear why <strong>Fire Emblem: Sacred Stones</strong> stands out as the premier entry point for anyone curious about strategy RPGs. Its approachable difficulty, dual‑protagonist narrative, and flexible class system provide a gentle learning curve while still rewarding mastery. Pair it with other GBA gems for a full‑spectrum retro experience, and you’ve got a compelling reason to fire up your browser today.</p>

